# tests/definitions/defs_common.rxtin — THE SHARED DEFINITIONS FILE.
#
# [DD-13b.W1.3] part 3, our own usage: pcrec's corpus composing over a
# library of its own, rather than only over fixtures written to exercise the
# format's grammar.
#
# A LIBRARY SHIPS NOTHING BY ITSELF (format_design §6.1): no `target` line,
# several blocks, so `pcrec --source` on this file builds nothing at exit 0.
# What it ships is NAMES.
#
# EACH DEFINITION IS WRITTEN TO EXERCISE ONE TIER of D89's three, so the
# composed artifacts have something to be right about:
#
#   `w`         NAMES and EXPORTS    -> DELIVERABLE: a delivering site gets
#               its group                a `groups[]` row `site.word`; a PLAIN
#                                        caller gets nothing and pays nothing
#   `num`       has no group at all  -> costs the caller nothing but the
#                                       wrapper's own internal number
#   `hostname`  NAMES and EXPORTS    -> the same, under whatever site a
#               its group                caller names
#   `dotted`    has capturing groups nothing reads and nothing exports ->
#                                       ERASED: each `A_CAP` is deleted and
#                                       spends NO number, which is what makes
#                                       the composed artifact's RX_NCAPS
#                                       smaller than a naive textual append's
#   `dd`        references its own group -> HIDDEN: a slot, no row, and it
#                                       survives because a group-number
#                                       reference inside a pattern always
#                                       works (D89 addendum point 1)
#
# [D89 addendum, 2026-09-03] NAMING A GROUP NO LONGER EXPORTS IT. Delivery is
# what a definition DECLARES with `export` and what a SITE asks for with
# `(?&site=name)`; the default is nothing exported and nothing delivered, so
# `dotted` and `dd` publish no interface at all and a caller of them pays for
# no slot they own.
#
# ITS EXTENSION IS `.rxtin` AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. `tests/harness/run.sh`
# finds `*.rxt`; a `.rxt` here would join the scored corpus and move four
# pinned census numbers (`tests/rxtsource/run_rxtsource_tests.sh`'s
# CENSUS_FILES/BLOCKS/LINES and the RUNSH_* it reconciles against). The
# identity proof beside this file copies these into a scratch directory as
# `.rxt` when it needs them, which is `tests/rxtsource/fixtures/`'s own
# convention.
description reusable pieces for the composition identity proof. Definitions only.

pattern (?<word>[a-z]+)
name w
export word

pattern [0-9]+
name num

pattern (?<host>[a-z]+(?:\.[a-z]+)+)
name hostname
export host

pattern ([a-z]+)\.([a-z]+)
name dotted

pattern (\d)\1
name dd
